From: luma-duo2 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] mutter: offer inexact scales on a handheld panel

The Duo 2's 1344x1892 panels want Android's density for them, scale 2.5,
which does not divide them exactly, so Mutter never offers it. Adds
patches/mutter/0030 (on a handheld, offer such scales with the logical size
rounded, verify a configuration of that size, never pick one by itself) to
Luma's Mutter series, under its own release.

diff --git a/patches/mutter/0000-luma-fedora-spec.patch b/patches/mutter/0000-luma-fedora-spec.patch
index 651b1c40..710a6ad9 100644
--- a/patches/mutter/0000-luma-fedora-spec.patch
+++ b/patches/mutter/0000-luma-fedora-spec.patch
@@ -1,11 +1,11 @@
 --- a/mutter.spec
 +++ b/mutter.spec
-@@ -29,13 +29,44 @@
+@@ -29,13 +29,45 @@
  
  Name:          mutter
  Version:       50.4
 -Release:       %autorelease
-+Release:       1.luma.20%{?dist}
++Release:       1.luma.20.duo2.1%{?dist}
  Summary:       Window and compositing manager based on Clutter
  
  # Automatically converted from old format: GPLv2+ - review is highly recommended.
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 +Patch1026:     0027-cogl-Scissor-journal-draws-to-what-they-cover.patch
 +Patch1027:     0028-clutter-actor-Do-not-redraw-the-whole-stage-for-a-first-paint.patch
 +Patch1028:     0029-stage-impl-Clip-compact-damage-with-the-scissor-alone.patch
